    rdf:value """at Orange, and after a quarrel over the Roman Arch, which Bernhard found more solid and grander than I did, we proceeded to be overwhelmed by the imposing façade of the Theatre. After exhausting that emotion, we ate some fruit, walked out to see a glorious sunset on Mt. Ventoux, smoked, and then took the train here.
Friday. Oct. 4. 1895. Avignon 
The thing to do would be to get rooms at the quiet  Europe , eat here, for the restaurant is not bad.
We spent a really rapturous day seeing this town and Villeneuve opposite, with its marvellous views. 
The Galleries are complete frauds, except for a small mask by Laurana. We had various letters - one from Perry saying he would send a Mr. Coba to see Bernhard - “He is """^^xsd:string ;
